1. Explain Bagging and Boosting methods. How is it different from each other.
Bagging:
Reduce variance by training multiple models independently on different random samples of the data.
How it works:
=>From the original dataset, create multiple bootstrap samples (random sampling with replacement).
=>Train a separate model (e.g., decision tree) on each sample.
Combine predictions:
=>Classification → Majority voting
=>Regression → Averaging
Key characteristics:
=>Models are trained in parallel
=>Reduces variance
=>Works best with high-variance models

Boosting:
Reduce bias by training models sequentially, where each model focuses on correcting the errors of the previous one.
How it works:
=>Start with a simple model.
=>Identify errors (misclassified points).
=>Give more weight/importance to those errors.
=>Train the next model focusing more on difficult cases.
=>Combine models (weighted sum or voting).
Key characteristics:
=>Models are trained sequentially (dependent on previous ones)
=>Reduces bias (improves underfitting)
=>Can be sensitive to noise and outliers

2. Explain how to handle imbalance in the data.
Handling imbalanced data (where one class heavily outweighs the other, like fraud vs normal transactions) is crucial—otherwise your model may look “accurate” but completely fail on the minority class.
Techniques to Handle Imbalance:
1. Data-Level Methods (Resampling)
a) Oversampling (increase minority class)
Duplicate or synthetically create minority samples
Popular method:
SMOTE
Pros:
Balances dataset without losing data
Cons:
Can cause overfitting (especially simple duplication)
b) Undersampling (reduce majority class)
Remove samples from majority class
Pros:
Faster training
Cons:
Loss of useful information
c) Hybrid methods
Combine both oversampling + undersampling
2. Algorithm-Level Methods
a) Use class weights
Assign higher penalty to minority class errors
Available in models like:
=>Logistic Regression
=>Support Vector Machine
b) Use ensemble techniques
Boosting methods handle imbalance better:
=>AdaBoost
=>Gradient Boosting
3. Evaluation Strategy
Instead of accuracy, use,
=>Confusion Matrix
=>Precision / Recall
=>F1-score
=>ROC-AUC
4. Threshold Tuning
=>Default threshold = 0.5
=>Adjust it to favor minority class
5. Anomaly Detection (for extreme imbalance)
Treat minority class as anomaly
Use models like:
=>Isolation Forest
=>One-Class SVM